# P5 FL19 alpha execution completion report V1

Status: ceremony-ready engineering release candidate; unexecuted.

Fable's missing-component findings were mechanically reproduced from exact
FL18 bytes before implementation: caller-supplied precondition digest echo; no
machine evaluator; no trial execution command; no persistent attempt writer;
no durable result seal; no Wave-1 active-time/checkpoint wiring; no output
firewall; no machine T1-first enforcement.

The FL19 implementation closes those gaps with schema v4 and three daemon
commands (`preconditions-evaluate`, `trial-execute`, `trial-status`).  No public
API accepts result JSON or scientific values.  All authority/execution commands
remain daemon-only, and direct mode fails closed.

Acceptance evidence:

- frozen set 20/20;
- machine preconditions and evidence binding PASS;
- digest echo CLOSED;
- T1 execution/LabelGate/seal PASS;
- W1 T1-first/174/resource/checkpoint/seal PASS;
- lifecycle, label ledger, durable writer and output firewall PASS;
- synthetic real-path E2E 24/24;
- original FL18 regressions 84/84;
- FL19 affected suites 87/87 (10 shell + 31 static + 15 functional + 31 targeted);
- PC7 synthetic/goldens 88/88 with deterministic double-run;
- migration replay 2/2;
- scientific estimand/adjudication/candidate/data/multiplicity changes all zero;
- real P5 labels read: NO;
- production authority mutations: 0;
- production cutover: NO.

The release intentionally carries no real-label input.  The TCB-bound adapter
contract requires later independent admin materialization beneath a fixed,
root-owned, daemon/k3-nonwritable data root.  This preserves the no-real-label
engineering boundary while making the execution interface and its failure
conditions ceremony-ready.

Final package manifest/self hashes are intentionally external to this report to
avoid a hash cycle.

